"entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 20, "start": 6, "tag": "DarkMatterDay"}], "urls": [{"description": "Happy #DarkMatterDay! There's more to the cosmos than meets the eye...", "display_url": "youtu.be/DvgfjMuPs00", "end": 251, "expanded_url": "https://youtu.be/DvgfjMuPs00", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116543906620084224/62RGfwt9?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116543906620084224/62RGfwt9?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 228, "status": 200, "title": "Muon g-2 | Whispers from dark matter", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DvgfjMuPs00&feature=youtu.be", "url": "https://t.co/qH3tU21s18"}]}, "id": "2116646647304245583", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 371, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "Happy #DarkMatterDay! There's more to the cosmos than meets the eye.\n\nThe precision of the Muon g-2 experiment at Fermilab makes it possible to listen for extremely faint signals from interactions between dark matter and muons.\nhttps://t.co/qH3tU21s18", "url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2116646647304245583"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:20:47.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116641560343540079"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/fcfyplusg/stat…", "end": 140, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/fcfyplusg/status/2116543354624262560", "start": 117, "url": "https://t.co/DYup1gETyt"}]}, "id": "2116641560343540079", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2079, "like_count": 46, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "repost_count": 4}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116543354624262560", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "LLMs are SO POWERFUL they traveled back in time to boost productive growth a few years before ChatGPT even launched: https://t.co/DYup1gETyt", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116641560343540079"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116638850109829120"]}, "author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:10:02.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116638852764844033"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 10, "start": 0, "tag": "Halloween"}, {"end": 254, "start": 235, "tag": "SciencePerspective"}], "urls": [{"description": "Reconstructing an injured muscle involves nuclear and mitochondrial contributions", "display_url": "scim.ag/3WW0iOs", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/3WW0iOs", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116638869495898112/1Uoev3Sg?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116638869495898112/1Uoev3Sg?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 256, "status": 200, "title": "Resealing and rebuilding injured muscle", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.abm2240?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=ownedSocial", "url": "https://t.co/b164yDk6Ju"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/M1BHOweTXD", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116638852764844033/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116638850109829120", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/M1BHOweTXD"}]}, "id": "2116638852764844033", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 5918, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "repost_count": 4}, "text": "#Halloween is usually filled with skeletons—but what about skeletal muscle? \n\nThis tissue is organized into elongated and aligned myofibers which, according to a 2021 study, can self-repair after localized damage. \n\nLearn more in this #SciencePerspective: https://t.co/b164yDk6Ju https://t.co/M1BHOweTXD", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116638852764844033"}, {"author_id": "272019676", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:00:08.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116636362023501949"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 22, "id": "4061566936", "start": 7, "username": "ChinaPowerCSIS"}]}, "id": "2116636362023501949", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 22, "id": "4061566936", "start": 7, "username": "ChinaPowerCSIS"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=vWcskm…", "end": 289, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vWcskmCxeOU", "start": 266, "url": "https://t.co/nbXJ8UjwEj"}]}, "text": "ICYMI: @ChinaPowerCSIS hosted the 10th anniversary of the China Power Conference. This year's event brought together leading experts for two days of discussion on core issues underpinning China's power and explored the current state of U.S.-China relations.\n\nWatch: https://t.co/nbXJ8UjwEj"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2215, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "ICYMI: @ChinaPowerCSIS hosted the 10th anniversary of the China Power Conference. This year's event brought together leading experts for two days of discussion on core issues underpinning China's power and explored the current state of U.S.-China relations.\n\nWatch:", "url": "https://x.com/CSIS/status/2116636362023501949"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116648413081047040"]}, "author_id": "166252256", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:48:02.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116648417229181250"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/zDDZ4tMeZr", "end": 47, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ENERGY/status/2116648417229181250/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116648413081047040", "start": 24, "url": "https://t.co/zDDZ4tMeZr"}]}, "id": "2116648417229181250", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2039, "like_count": 83, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "repost_count": 22}, "text": "Spooky szn is upon us 👻 https://t.co/zDDZ4tMeZr", "url": "https://x.com/ENERGY/status/2116648417229181250"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116639095141093376"]}, "author_id": "16933019", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:11:05.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116639118679744731"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/5n7f2fTDZP", "end": 35, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AukeHoekstra/status/2116639118679744731/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116639095141093376", "start": 12, "url": "https://t.co/5n7f2fTDZP"}]}, "id": "2116639118679744731", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 895, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "Just sayin' https://t.co/5n7f2fTDZP", "url": "https://x.com/AukeHoekstra/status/2116639118679744731"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116631363206168576"]}, "author_id": "4939401", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:02:32.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116633906749563016", "2116634022608867660", "2116636967517798672"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/UvfaN0lYwX", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/patrickc/status/2116636967517798672/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116631363206168576", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/UvfaN0lYwX"}]}, "id": "2116636967517798672", "note_tweet": {"text": "I'm now building an \"improvements\" feature into all of my personal vibecoded applications: a freeform text input that's hooked up to an agent that yolo implements whatever is submitted.\n\nIt's an interesting experience -- the activation energy barrier to sanding any rough edge or implementing any new feature becomes extremely low. Someone else who uses one of the applications I created has already implemented 150 improvements over the course of a few days. This pattern feels like a new kind of tool -- liquid software? -- and every application that doesn't have this feature now has a slightly rigid and anachronistic flavor. Why can't I just tell it how I want it to be different?\n\nNow, it's not obvious to me how this pattern can or should scale. Does it become unmaintainable after a while? (Maybe model intelligence improvement outstrips my feature appetite such that it's fine?) How does collaborative software work in this model? Can software designed this way be secure and reliable?\n\nWhatever the larger questions about broader deployment, it definitely works great in a personal context. It reminds me a little of the visions of Lisp/Lisp machines, Smalltalk, and HyperCard -- systems that the user can take control of and modify. Those visions never quite worked, though: the vast majority of software today is not end-user modifiable in any useful way. So, while this \"liquid\" affordance is a very small touch, the way it changes one's relation to the software feels a bit transgressive and empowering in a Lickliderian and Engelbartian way."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 295, "impression_count": 21638, "like_count": 389, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 65, "repost_count": 11}, "text": "I'm now building an \"improvements\" feature into all of my personal vibecoded applications: a freeform text input that's hooked up to an agent that yolo implements whatever is submitted.\n\nIt's an interesting experience -- the activation energy barrier to sanding any rough edge or https://t.co/UvfaN0lYwX", "url": "https://x.com/patrickc/status/2116636967517798672"}, {"author_id": "626660983", "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:59:36.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116636229504823514"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/lillybilly299/…", "end": 44, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/lillybilly299/status/2116544731614212158", "start": 21, "url": "https://t.co/0ssJqgYAhp"}]}, "id": "2116636229504823514", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1422, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "repost_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116544731614212158", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It’s called “a meal” https://t.co/0ssJqgYAhp", "url": "https://x.com/lymanstoneky/status/2116636229504823514"}, {"author_id": "1797337858140753920", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:56:45.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2116650611286712473"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 163, 